@Node Intro "--> Features <--"

 * displays nearly all informations avaible for the user on one screen 
 * nice ANSI output                                                   
 * running on all Express Versions (/X 2.xx-3.xx & Sigma Express)     
 * no backdoors
 * compiled AREXX
 * tested over monthes

 
                           @{" Back to main menu " link "MAIN"}
@endnode
@Node Install "--> Installation <--"

 Extract the whole Dream Status archiv to you assigned doors dir.

 /X2.x: Append the following Line to your
        BBS:Commands/BBS.CMD File:
        ---------------------->> Cut Here <<--------------------------
        *S            RM010DOORS:DreamStatus/DreamStatus.rexx
        ---------------------->> Cut Here <<--------------------------

 /X3.x: For installing on that systems make your own Icon and place it
        in your BBS:Commands/BBS.CMD drawer.

 Copy the rexxsupport.library to your assigned LIBS: dir.

 If the BBS name is not displayed correctly, insert it in the file
 DreamStatus.CFG. Do not use Escape Codes for colors, bold, underlined,..
 and not more than 24 figures!

 DreamStatus.CFG - The Config File:
 Edit the names and paths of the User.Keys file, Systemstats file,
 Computerlist file and if needed the BBS Name.
 Note: /X v3.xx users have to edit the included Computerlist file for
       their own System. In the first line stands the amount of
       Computers, after that each Computer.

 Be sure, that you have the following files: (otherwise the door won`t work)
 * LIBS:rexxsupport.library
 * Doors:DreamStatus/DreamStatus.cfg
 * USER.KEYS
 * SystemStats
 * Computerlist


                           @{" Back to main menu " link "MAIN"}
@endnode
